- bge-reranker-v2-minicpm-layerwise: 5. This is the default value.

> Chunking example
> - If you use the bge-reranker-v2-minicpm-layerwise model, the maximum single inference window is 2,048 tokens. If the query is 48 tokens and a single document parameter contains 9,000 tokens, the document is split into chunks: tokens 1 to 2,000 form the first chunk, tokens 2,001 to 4,000 form the second chunk, and so on. If the number of chunks exceeds the value of MaxChunksPerDoc, the subsequent text is discarded.', example='10', position='Body'),
  model?: string(name='Model', description='The rerank model. Valid values:
- bge-reranker-v2-m3: provides good performance and supports up to 8,192 tokens for a single inference. Text that exceeds this limit is split into chunks, which may degrade performance. This is the default value.
- bge-reranker-v2-minicpm-layerwise: provides better performance than bge-reranker-v2-m3 and supports up to 2,048 tokens for a single inference. Text that exceeds this limit is split into chunks, which may degrade performance.', example='bge-reranker-v2-m3', position='Body'),
